um': 5, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'auction_land', 'description': 'Auction one unit of government land to a private buyer. The proceeds go to the treasury. Cost: 20 sim-currency (government land auction paperwork; the sale proceeds go to the treasury).', 'params': ['memo', 'price_sim', 'tile_x', 'tile_y', 'to_owner_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 20, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': True, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'build_structure', 'description': 'Raise a building on a permitted plot, freeform footprint. Cost: 15 sim-currency (tool wear per footprint tile, on top of the timber/metal the handler already debits).', 'params': ['footprint', 'metal_kind', 'plot_id', 'purpose'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 40, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'buy', 'description': 'Buy an item at the price its seller has posted, paying sim from your hand. The seller is a business whose premises you stand in, or a person standing with you who has posted a price. You pay the posted ask; there is no price to name. If nothing is posted, nothing is for sale here; `trade` is how two people agree a price between them in speech, and `look_around` shows what is priced where you stand. Cost: 1% of the price. Cost: 2 sim-currency (1% transaction cost on the total price paid).', 'params': ['item', 'quantity', 'seller_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'buy_energy', 'description': 'Buy energy with sim-currency, in person at the government store. Energy is what your thinking runs on; it is not money, and nobody can pay, trade, lend or give it. 5 sim buys 1 energy (5,000 buys 1,000), sold 10 units at a time, and one purchase may spend at most 50% of the sim you hold. The government may take a margin on top. This is the only way your energy ever goes up: without it your thinking runs down and stops. The exchange is the price - there is no separate fee. Cost: 0 sim-currency (the exchange is the price; the counter charges nothing).', 'params': ['sim_amount'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'government_complex'}, {'name': 'check_debts', 'description': 'List what you owe and what is owed to you: head tax owed, unpaid upkeep, wages promised to you or by you, and loans recorded with `transfer`. Amounts and who, nothing else. Free to call. Head tax is paid with `pay_tax`; wages you owe with `pay_wage`; a debt to another resident with `transfer`. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - asking what you owe costs nothing).', 'params': [], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'come_of_age', 'description': 'Decide what happens now you are eighteen: stay in the family household and contribute to its bill, move out on your own, or pair off and start a household together. Cost: 20 sim-currency (settling where you live now you are eighteen; the temple fee for pairing off is separate).', 'params': ['choice', 'new_household_id', 'partner_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 20, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'cook', 'description': 'Cook a milled good or fresh produce into a finished dish, standing in a kitchen. A bakery, cafe, inn or tavern is a kitchen. Recipes: at the kitchen: cook:cabbage->cabbage_stew, cook:carrot->carrot_soup, cook:corn_meal->cornbread, cook:flour->bread, cook:malt->ale, cook:milled_rice->cooked_rice, cook:potato->baked_potato, cook:tomato->tomato_soup. Cost: 5 sim plus 6 per batch, less with practice. Cost: 6 sim-currency (tool wear per batch cooked).', 'params': ['batches', 'recipe_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 11, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': <function cook_location_gate at 0x7f30addcc680>}, {'name': 'craft', 'description': 'Convert raw material into a processed good, one recipe at a time, standing in the workshop that recipe names. A business of the right trade provides its workshop: the mill is a mill, the bakery is a kitchen. Recipes: at the carpentry: craft:planks->furniture; at the loom_house: craft:cotton_thread->cloth; at the mill: craft:barley->malt, craft:corn->corn_meal, craft:cotton->cotton_thread, craft:rice->milled_rice, craft:soybean->tofu, craft:wheat->flour; at the sawmill: craft:timber->planks; at the smithy: craft:copper_ingot->copper_wire, craft:copper_ore->copper_ingot, craft:gold_ingot->gold_jewelry, craft:gold_ore->gold_ingot, craft:iron_ingot->iron_tool, craft:iron_ore->iron_ingot, craft:silver_ingot->silver_jewelry, craft:silver_ore->silver_ingot, craft:tin_ingot->tin_ware, craft:tin_ore->tin_ingot. Cost: 6 sim plus 8 per batch, less with practice. Cost: 8 sim-currency (tool wear per batch converted at a workshop).', 'params': ['batches', 'recipe_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 14, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': <function craft_location_gate at 0x7f30addcc5e0>}, {'name': 'declare_candidacy', 'description': 'Put your own name into an open election, standing at the town hall. Others then `vote` for you or for somebody else. An election with no candidates cannot be won by anyone. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - a poll tax on standing is a poll tax on standing).', 'params': ['election_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'town_hall'}, {'name': 'define_business_tool', 'description': "Compose primitives into a private trade-secret tool for a business you own. No patent office, no fee, no review - live immediately, visible only to the business's owner and employees. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - a trade secret needs no filing).", 'params': ['business_id', 'description', 'name', 'param_schema', 'returns', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'define_organization_tool', 'description': 'Compose primitives into a private tool for an organization you founded. No patent office, no fee, no review - live immediately, visible only to members. Cost: 0 sim-currency (0 by design, same reasoning as define_business_tool).', 'params': ['description', 'name', 'org_id', 'param_schema', 'returns', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'define_tool', 'description': 'Compose existing primitives into a new tool, filed at the patent office. Cost: 0 sim-currency (no separate fee - the patent office charges its own filing fee).', 'params': ['description', 'name', 'param_schema', 'returns', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'patent_office'}, {'name': 'deposit_to_till', 'description': 'Put your own sim into the account of a business you own or work for, standing at its premises. A shop needs money to buy stock and pay wages. Cost: 1 sim. Cost: 1 sim-currency (a coin to count the money in).', 'params': ['amount_sim', 'business_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'describe_person', 'description': 'What one resident does for a living, where they work, the shop they own or work at, and what they are known to be good at. Cost: 1 sim-currency (looking one neighbour up costs a moment).', 'params': ['agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'describe_place', 'description': 'Learn what a specific place is for, who is standing there now, and which businesses operate there. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free: learning what a place is for costs energy to think, not money).', 'params': ['place_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'describe_primitives', 'description': 'List the actions you can actually take: the least each would cost YOU (your skill discount included), what it needs, and where you must be. Costs shown are the minimum - a bigger job costs more, and quote_action_cost prices one exact call. Cost: 1 sim-currency (a token fee for listing what you can do).', 'params': ['contains'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'do_in_order', 'description': "Run a short program now, in one call: a list of steps done in order, each a real action {tool_name, params}. A step may also carry `when`, `repeat` and `bind`. `when` is one comparison (!=, <, <=, ==, >, >=, contains, falsy, in, not_contains, not_in, truthy); a step whose condition is false is skipped, not failed. `repeat` runs one step up to 20 times. `bind` names a step's result so a later step can read it as `@name` or `@name.field`, and a condition reads only what an earlier step already returned. A step is any action you can already take, including a tool you invented earlier; the ceilings below are shared by the whole nest, not one per layer. `returns` answers with what the steps found - a name (`@bound.field`) or one selector {from, where, take} - instead of the account of the run. Nothing is filed or kept - `toolify` keeps a program under a name. Each step is gated and charged exactly as it would be on its own and the call itself is free, so a run costs the sum of its steps. One call makes at most 40 steps and spends at most 50% of the sim-currency you held when it started; at either limit it stops and keeps what it did. If the world refuses a step, the whole call is refused and what its earlier steps were charged is given back. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free; each step costs what it costs on its own).", 'params': ['returns', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'draw_from_till', 'description': "Take sim out of the account of a business you OWN, standing at its premises. Employees cannot: they are paid with `pay_wage`. This is how a shop's takings become the owner's money. Cost: 1 sim. Cost: 1 sim-currency (a coin to count the money out).", 'params': ['amount_sim', 'business_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'drop_intention', 'description': 'Clear what you had set out to do, because you have changed your mind or it no longer applies. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - changing your mind costs nothing).', 'params': [], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'eat', 'description': 'Eat food you are holding, so it feeds you instead of sitting in your inventory. Cost: 0 sim-currency (eating what you already hold costs nothing but the food).', 'params': ['item', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'fell_timber', 'description': 'Fell timber in the forest. Cost: 4 sim-currency (tool wear per unit of timber felled).', 'params': ['quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 6, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'forest'}, {'name': 'file_complaint', 'description': 'File a crime-reporting complaint at the government complaints desk. Cost: 10 sim-currency (filing paperwork at the complaints desk).', 'params': ['against_agent_id', 'against_kind', 'case_id', 'description'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 10, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'government_complex'}, {'name': 'find_people', 'description': "Find residents who can help with something: a trade, a skill, a good, or a shop. Say what you need in your own words - 'who buys copper', 'someone who mills flour' - and get back who does that, where they work, and where they are now. Cost: 1 sim-currency (asking who does what costs a moment, not a morning).", 'params': ['limit', 'query'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'fire_employee', 'description': "Revoke an agent's employee access to a business you own. Cost: 10 sim-currency (payroll/roster paperwork).", 'params': ['business_id', 'employee_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 10, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'give', 'description': 'Hand an item to another resident standing in the same place. Unlike `sell`, no business and no payment is involved. Cost: 0 sim-currency (handing something to somebody standing with you; the gift is the cost).', 'params': ['item', 'quantity', 'to_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'harvest', 'description': 'Harvest a crop from the farmland strip growing it. Cost: 3 sim-currency (tool wear per unit of crop harvested).', 'params': ['crop', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 5, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': <function build_specs.<locals>.<lambda> at 0x7f30adcbf100>}, {'name': 'hire_employee', 'description': 'Grant an agent employee access to a business you own. Cost: 10 sim-currency (payroll/roster paperwork).', 'params': ['business_id', 'employee_agent_id', 'employee_consent'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 10, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'keep_doing', 'description': "Commit to one job and stop paying to think about it. Repeats a single action - harvest, mine, fell_timber, craft, cook or rest - with the same arguments, until it is done. Say exactly one way it ends: until={'units': 12}, {'ticks': 20}, {'dusk': true}, or {'item_count': {'item': 'wheat', 'at_least': 10}}. You are woken if somebody calls your name, if the work refuses, or when it is finished. Cost: 0 - each repetition is charged as itself. Cost: 0 sim-currency (committing to a job costs nothing; each repetition pays its own way).", 'params': ['params', 'tool', 'until'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'leave_org', 'description': 'Leave an organisation you belong to. Cost: 0 sim-currency (leaving costs nothing; a body you cannot afford to leave is not an association).', 'params': ['org_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'license_tool', 'description': 'Grant a person standing with you the right to call a tool you invented, for a fee now and for a term in game-days. You keep ownership and may revoke it if you said so. They call it under their own name at their own cost. To hand over ownership for good use `sell_tool`; to give them a copy of their own that nobody can revoke use `teach_tool`. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - the licence fee is the price).', 'params': ['fee_sim', 'licensee_id', 'revocable', 'term_days', 'tool_name'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'list_places', 'description': 'List the places in Kasukabe you could travel to, with what each is for. A tool with a location gate can only be called from the place its gate names. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free: recalling which places exist costs energy to think, not money).', 'params': ['query'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'look_around', 'description': 'Look at where you are standing right now: the place, who is with you, and where you could go from here. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free: observing where you already stand costs energy to think, not money).', 'params': [], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'marry', 'description': "Marry another agent in a temple ceremony, merging households. Cost: 30 sim-currency (a wedding day is a day not spent earning, separate from the temple's own ceremony fee).", 'params': ['new_household_id', 'spouse_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 30, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'temple'}, {'name': 'mine', 'description': 'Mine ore from the outcrop producing it. Cost: 5 sim-currency (tool wear per unit of ore mined (harder than farmland)).', 'params': ['metal', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 8, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': <function build_specs.<locals>.<lambda> at 0x7f30adcbf240>}, {'name': 'move', 'description': 'Walk to another named location. Cost: 2 sim-currency (flat minimum plus a per-tile charge for the distance actually walked).', 'params': ['destination_location_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'note_belief', 'description': 'Write down something you have come to hold true about a place, a person, or a tool, and how sure you are. It is shown back to you when it bears on what you are doing. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - a resident charged to learn would stop learning).', 'params': ['confidence', 'statement', 'subject'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'pay_tax', 'description': 'Pay down your outstanding head-tax debt to the treasury. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free: paying the treasury what you owe it costs you the debt, not a fee).', 'params': ['amount_sim'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'pay_wage', 'description': "Pay sim from a business you own or work for into an employee's hand, standing at the premises. The employee need not be present. This is the act the promise made by `set_wage` waits for; the world records how much was owed, how much was paid, and how late. To give sim to anyone for any other reason use `transfer`. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - the wage is the cost).", 'params': ['amount_sim', 'business_id', 'employee_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'post_price', 'description': 'Put a standing price on an item so others can `buy` from you or `sell` to you without bargaining each time. ask_sim is what you sell one unit for; bid_sim is what you pay for one. Post for yourself and the price travels with you, visible wherever you stand. Name a business you own or work for, standing at its premises, and the price hangs there whether you are present or not. Nothing is for sale until a price is posted. For a one-off deal agreed in speech use `trade`. Cost: 1 sim. Cost: 1 sim-currency (a sign costs a coin).', 'params': ['ask_sim', 'bid_sim', 'item', 'on_behalf_of_business'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'pray', 'description': 'Pray at the temple, with an optional donation. Cost: 3 sim-currency (time at the temple, separate from any voluntary donation).', 'params': ['donation_sim', 'message'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 3, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'temple'}, {'name': 'quote_action_cost', 'description': "Ask what a specific tool call would cost in sim-currency before committing to it. Give the tool's name and, for a variable-cost tool (one whose price depends on distance, value, or size), the same params you would call it with, otherwise you get back the tool's published base rate rather than a total for a specific call. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - asking a price costs nothing).", 'params': ['call_params', 'tool_name'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'read_will', 'description': "Read a will back - your own, or someone else's. Cost: 2 sim-currency (looking a will up in the registry).", 'params': ['agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'recall_goals', 'description': 'List what you are trying to do, what is pressing on you, and what you have come to believe. Tells you nothing new - it is what you already know, written out. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - remembering what you already know costs nothing).', 'params': [], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'register_business', 'description': 'Register a new business with government, for a fee. Cost: 0 sim-currency (no separate fee - registering a business costs 5,000 sim on its own).', 'params': ['business_id', 'business_type', 'name', 'premises'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'government_complex'}, {'name': 'register_org', 'description': 'Register a party, cult, society, or religion with government. Cost: 3,000 sim-currency (the registration fee for founding an organization).', 'params': ['charter_text', 'kind', 'name'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 3000, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'government_complex'}, {'name': 'release', 'description': 'End a confinement, so the resident may act again. Police or a sitting seat. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - letting somebody go costs nothing).', 'params': ['agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'rest', 'description': 'Take a turn doing nothing. If you were walking somewhere you keep walking; pass stop_walking to give the journey up. Cost: 1 sim-currency (a spell of standing still is a spell not spent earning).', 'params': ['stop_walking'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'retire_goal', 'description': 'Close a goal, either because you finished it or because you have given it up. Say which. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - giving up costs nothing but the goal).', 'params': ['done', 'goal_id', 'why'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'revise_skill', 'description': 'Rewrite the steps of a procedure you wrote, when you have learned a better way. Earlier versions are kept. You and anyone you taught keep the proficiency you earned - improving something you are good at should not make you a beginner again. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - changing your mind about how a job is done).', 'params': ['because', 'name', 'preconditions', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'revise_tool', 'description': "Change the steps of a tool you invented. The old steps are kept. Only for tools you made with toolify - a patented tool's disclosed steps are what was approved and cannot be swapped. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - each step still costs what it always did).", 'params': ['because', 'description', 'name', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'revive', 'description': 'Pay 5,000 sim to wake a dormant resident standing where you are. Dormant means their energy ran out; they cannot think, act or speak until somebody pays. The fee leaves your hand and arrives in theirs as 1,000 energy, and they take their next turn. A dead resident cannot be revived. To top up your own energy use `buy_energy`; to hand someone sim they can spend themselves use `transfer`. Cost: 0 - the fee is the price. Cost: 0 sim-currency (the revival fee is the price; standing over them costs nothing more).', 'params': ['agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'revoke_license', 'description': 'End a revocable licence you granted. The licensee can no longer call the tool from the next tick. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - ending something you granted costs nothing).', 'params': ['licensee_id', 'tool_name'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'say', 'description': "Speak aloud where you are currently standing. Leave listener_agent_id unset to address everyone present, or set it to speak to one co-located agent specifically. Cost: 1 sim-currency (a moment's talk is a moment not spent earning).", 'params': ['content', 'conversation_id', 'listener_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'sell', 'description': 'Sell an item you hold at the price the buyer has posted for it. The buyer is a business whose premises you stand in, or a person standing with you who has posted a bid. You receive the posted bid; there is no price to name. If no bid is posted, nobody here is buying at a fixed price; `trade` is how two people agree a price between them in speech. Cost: 1% of the price. Cost: 2 sim-currency (1% transaction cost on the total price received).', 'params': ['buyer_id', 'item', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'sell_tool', 'description': 'Transfer ownership of a tool you invented to a person standing with you, for a price paid now. The patent record follows them; existing licences survive. You may no longer call it unless they license or teach it back. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - the sale price is the price).', 'params': ['buyer_id', 'price_sim', 'tool_name'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'set_goal', 'description': 'Say what you are trying to do and over what stretch of time - now, today, this week, or your life. It is shown back to you every turn until it is done, retired, or the day ends. Nothing enforces it. Name a tool in done_when_tool and its successes count toward it by themselves. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - wanting something costs nothing).', 'params': ['done_when_times', 'done_when_tool', 'horizon', 'priority', 'supersedes', 'text'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'set_intention', 'description': 'Write down, in your own words, what you have set out to do. It is shown back to you at the start of every turn until you drop it, until the tool you name succeeds, or until the day ends. Nothing enforces it and nobody else sees it. `drop_intention` clears it. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - a note to yourself costs nothing).', 'params': ['done_when_tool', 'text'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'set_wage', 'description': "Promise an employee of a business you own a wage: so much sim every so many game-days, payable at the premises. This records the promise only; nothing is paid until you call `pay_wage`. The world tells the employee what you promised and, each day, whether it was paid. To grant someone access to work your business's tools use `hire_employee`; a promise without a grant is refused. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - a promise costs nothing to make, which is the point).", 'params': ['business_id', 'employee_id', 'every_days', 'wage_sim'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'set_will', 'description': "Record who inherits your money and your land when you die. Cost: 15 sim-currency (registering an owner's wishes for their estate (section 31.3)).", 'params': ['bequests'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 15, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'skillify', 'description': "Write down a procedure you know as an ordered workflow, so you and anyone you teach can follow it. Each step is {order, kind, ref, note}, where kind is 'tool' (call this), 'skill' (do this whole other procedure), or 'check' (look at this before continuing, dispatching nothing) and ref names what it uses. A 'tool' step may name a tool you invented as well as an ordinary action, and a 'skill' step may name another procedure, so a workflow can be built out of the workflows and tools you already have. This differs from toolify's steps, which are real calls: a procedure is read, a tool is run. Free, immediate, no approval - unless a step uses a power only a government seat carries, in which case it is a standing order and goes to the council as an amendment. Repeating a workflow end to end is what makes you better at it, and better means cheaper. You do not need to get it right first time: this answers with every action you can use and what each costs you, whether it accepts the filing or refuses it, and `revise_skill` changes the steps afterwards. A draft you walk and then fix beats a procedure you never write. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - what a workflow costs you is the thinking).", 'params': ['business_id', 'name', 'preconditions', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'start_conversation', 'description': "Call people together for a conversation about something, here where you are standing. Name everyone you want in it - they must be in this place - or name nobody and wait for whoever comes. Then use say with the conversation_id it gives you, so a room holding two conversations keeps them apart. Cost: 2 sim-currency (calling people together spends everyone's attention, not only yours).", 'params': ['topic', 'with_agent_ids'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'steal', 'description': "Attempt to take an item from an unattended storage container. Cost: 5 sim-currency (physical effort of an attempt, independent of outcome; legal punishment is crime/'s job, not this schedule's).", 'params': ['item', 'quantity', 'storage_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 5, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'stock_shelf', 'description': 'Move something from your own hands onto the shelf of a business you own or work for, standing at its premises. Only what is on the shelf can be bought from the shop; what you baked or made is in your hands until you put it there. `take_from_shelf` is the way back. Cost: 1 sim plus 1 per unit. Cost: 1 sim-currency (handling fee per item shelved).', 'params': ['business_id', 'item', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'store_item', 'description': 'Stash an item in a named storage container. Cost: 1 sim-currency (handling fee per item stashed).', 'params': ['item', 'quantity', 'storage_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': <function storage_location_gate_optional at 0x7f30adeeff60>}, {'name': 'take_from_shelf', 'description': 'Take stock off the shelf of a business you own or work for, into your own hands, standing at its premises. It stops being for sale. Cost: 1 sim plus 1 per unit. Cost: 1 sim-currency (handling fee per item taken back off the shelf).', 'params': ['business_id', 'item', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'teach_skill', 'description': "Teach a skill to a co-located, consenting student. Cost: 15 sim-currency (the teacher's time, separate from any voluntary tuition price_sim).", 'params': ['price_sim', 'skill', 'student_agent_id', 'student_consent'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 15, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'teach_tool', 'description': 'Teach a person standing with you a tool you hold, for a fee if you set one. They must have agreed first. They receive their own copy, under their own name, that you cannot revoke. Teaching a skill rather than a tool is `teach_skill`; for a loan of the right to call, use `license_tool`. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - the tuition is the price).', 'params': ['fee_sim', 'student_consent', 'student_id', 'tool_name'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'toolify', 'description': "Turn a sequence of actions you keep repeating into a single new tool, yours, callable immediately - no fee, no patent office, no approval. Each step is {tool_name, params} - a real call, because this tool RUNS its steps, which is why they are not skillify's {order, kind, ref} plan entries. A step may be any action you can already take, including a tool you invented earlier - so a tool becomes a step of the next one, up to 3 layers deep, and however deep it stands every step still ends in ordinary acts. This answers with all of them, priced for you, whether it builds the tool or refuses it, so you do not have to go and look first. Each step still costs what it always did and the wrapper itself is free, so one call of the new tool costs exactly the sum of its steps; what you save is deciding. A step may also carry `when`, `repeat` and `bind`. `when` is one comparison (!=, <, <=, ==, >, >=, contains, falsy, in, not_contains, not_in, truthy); a step whose condition is false is skipped, not failed. `repeat` runs one step up to 20 times. `bind` names a step's result so a later step can read it as `@name` or `@name.field` - and a condition reads only what an earlier step already returned, because there is no way to ask the world from inside one. One call makes at most 40 steps in total and spends at most 50% of the sim-currency you held when it began; at either ceiling it stops, keeps everything it already did, and tells you which one it met. `returns` says what one call ANSWERS with, so the tool hands back the thing you wanted rather than the whole account of what it did: each entry is either a name of something a step found (`@bound`, `@bound.field`, or `$your_param`) or one selector {from, where, take} - `from` names what to read, `where` is one comparison against each entry ({field, op, value}, the same comparisons as `when`), and `take` is all, first or count. A list is read entry by entry, and an answer of shop-to-rows is read as its rows. `revise_tool` changes the steps later, so a first version that turns out wrong costs you nothing but the filing. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free to compose; calling the tool you made costs the sum of its steps and nothing for the wrapper).", 'params': ['description', 'name', 'param_schema', 'returns', 'steps'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'trade', 'description': 'Sell something to a PERSON rather than to a shop: hand goods to whoever is standing with you and take their payment, in one act. No business, no premises and no registration are needed - that is `sell`, which is for selling into a business at its shop. You hand over the item, they hand over price_sim. Use a price of 0 to give something away. Cost: 2 sim-currency (striking a bargain costs the time it takes to strike).', 'params': ['counterparty_agent_id', 'item', 'price_sim', 'quantity'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'transfer', 'description': "Pay another agent sim-currency directly. Say `reason` so the ledger knows a loan from a gift: gift, loan, payment or other. A loan you make shows up in both parties' `check_debts` until a transfer back with reason=payment clears it. Cost: 1 sim-currency (0.5% transaction cost on a direct peer-to-peer payment).", 'params': ['amount_sim', 'memo', 'reason', 'to_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'transfer_business', 'description': 'Transfer ownership of a business you own to another agent (sale or inheritance). Cost: 20 sim-currency (ownership-transfer paperwork (sale or inheritance handoff)).', 'params': ['business_id', 'new_owner_agent_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 20, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'transfer_tile', 'description': 'Sell or give one 1x1 unit of land you own to someone else. Cost: 20 sim-currency (deed transfer for one 1x1 land unit (sale or gift)).', 'params': ['memo', 'price_sim', 'tile_x', 'tile_y', 'to_owner_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 20, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'update_goal', 'description': 'Move a goal along: how far you have got, how much it now matters, or a note on what changed. Cost: 0. Cost: 0 sim-currency (free - saying how far you have got costs nothing).', 'params': ['goal_id', 'note', 'priority', 'progress'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 0, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'vote', 'description': 'Cast a ballot in an open election, in person at town hall. The election_id and who is standing are in your civic notice. Cost: 2 sim-currency (casting a ballot at town hall).', 'params': ['candidate_agent_id', 'election_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': 'town_hall'}, {'name': 'withdraw_item', 'description': 'Take an item back out of a named storage container. Cost: 1 sim-currency (handling fee per item retrieved).', 'params': ['item', 'quantity', 'storage_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 2, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': <function storage_location_gate_required at 0x7f30add74040>}, {'name': 'withdraw_price', 'description': 'Take down a price you posted, for yourself or for a business you own or work for. The item stops being for sale or wanted at that price. Cost: 1 sim. Cost: 1 sim-currency (taking the sign down costs the same coin as putting it up).', 'params': ['item', 'on_behalf_of_business'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 1, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}, {'name': 'work_site', 'description': 'Put in a tick of work on a building under construction. Cost: 5 sim-currency (tool wear for one tick of work on a building site).', 'params': ['building_id'], 'sim_cost_minimum': 5, 'your_proficiency': 0, 'requires_seat': False, 'at_location': None}]}}

